# Backend Code Patterns

## Controller Rules
1. **THIN** - chỉ handle req/res, delegate to services
2. Always `try/catch` hoặc pass errors to `next()`
3. Use `req.body` sau khi đã validate (Zod inferred type)
4. Return consistent response format
5. Không gọi trực tiếp Prisma - phải qua service

```typescript
// ✅ Controller template
export const handlerName = async (
  req: Request<Params, ResBody, ReqBody>,
  res: Response<ApiResponse<ResBody>>,
  next: NextFunction
): Promise<void> => {
  try {
    const result = await service.method(req.body);
    res.status(200).json({ success: true, data: result });
  } catch (error) {
    next(error);
  }
};
```

## Service Rules
1. **THICK** - chứa business logic
2. Throw custom errors, không return error objects
3. Orchestrate multiple repositories
4. Emit events cho decoupled logic
5. Inject dependencies qua constructor

```typescript
export class PostService {
  constructor(
    private postRepo: PostRepository,
    private userRepo: UserRepository,
    private eventBus: EventEmitter,
  ) {}

  async create(authorId: string, dto: CreatePostDTO): Promise<Post> {
    const author = await this.userRepo.findById(authorId);
    if (!author) throw new NotFoundError('User');

    const post = await this.postRepo.create({ ...dto, authorId });
    this.eventBus.emit('post.created', post);

    return post;
  }
}
```

## Repository Rules
1. **ONLY** place gọi Prisma
2. Return domain types, không return raw Prisma types
3. Methods tên rõ ràng: `findById`, `findByEmail`, `createMany`
4. No business logic - chỉ data access

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
async findActiveUsers(): Promise<User[]> {
  return this.prisma.user.findMany({ where: { isActive: true } });
}

// ❌ BAD - business logic in repo
async findActiveUsersWithFriends(): Promise<User[]> {
  const users = await this.prisma.user.findMany({ where: { isActive: true } });
  return users.filter(u => u.friends.length > 0);
}
```

## Response Format
```typescript
// Success
{
  "success": true,
  "data": T,
  "meta"?: { page, limit, total } // for pagination
}

// Error
{
  "success": false,
  "error": {
    "message": string,
    "code"?: string,
    "details"?: unknown
  }
}
```

## Async Patterns
```typescript
// ✅ Parallel
const [user, posts] = await Promise.all([
  userRepo.findById(id),
  postRepo.findByUserId(id),
]);

// ✅ Sequential when dependent
const user = await userRepo.findById(id);
if (!user) throw new NotFoundError('User');
const profile = await profileRepo.findByUserId(user.id);
```
